> > > ln p(theta,phi|w,alpha,beta = sum_{m=1}^M ln (Dirichlet(theta_m|alpha)) + sum_{k=K}^M ln (Dirichlet(phi_k|beta)) + sum_{m=1}^M sum_{n=1}^{N[m]} ln (sum_{z=1}^K Categorical(z|theta_m) * Categorical(w_{m,n}|phi_z))
> > >
> > > which reassuringly matches the math in the link that you gave in your 2012 post (http://lingpipe-blog.com/2011/04/14/summing-out-topic-assignments-ld/)
> > >
> > > Yet in the Stan code provided in the reference manual, unless I'm missing something, the likelihood constructs the first two pieces and not the third (suppressing summations):
> > >
> > > ln (Dirichlet(theta_m|alpha)) <=> log(theta[doc[n],k])
> > > ln (Dirichlet(phi_k|beta)) <=> log(phi[k,w[n]])
> > > ln (sum_{z=1}^K Categorical(z|theta_m) * Categorical(w_{m,n}|phi_z)) <=> ???
