>
> - Bob
>
> On Sep 14, 2014, at 7:16 AM, Martin Šmíra <smira....@gmail.com> wrote:
>
>> Hi Stan,
>>
>> I'm translating another model from the Bayesian Cognitive Modeling book from chapter Heuristic Decision Making.
>>
>> The model of interest is called Search and is just a simple extension of model TTB (Take-the-best), which I implemented easily. I'll send a link for this model too, the code is not complicated so I hope there is no need to explain it.
>>
>> Problem starts when I extend the model for individual "search order" - parameter s. The parameter will take rank values from 1 to 9, different for each subject ns. The prior for s should be uniform for each of the combination (9!), in WinBUGS prior is implemented using tempory parameter stemp ~ N(0, sqrt(1000)) which is then ranked. In Stan I tried to do it in similar way either by using function rank or sort_indices_asc. Is there a better way in Stan to give prior to parameter s?
>>
>> Problem is that the model doesn't converge and is not mixing variable s properly. There is also small problem with indexing ttb[] which is done with t[ns,nq]. I used conditional statements in this case, but I also tried to solve it in different ways, but it didn't really help the performance. I don't this is the bottleneck here.
>>
>> Here are models - former TTB model, my attempt for the extended model, both models in Jags and also data in .Rdata format:
>> https://github.com/neekro/Stan_translate/tree/master/Heuristic%20decision-making
>>
