Hi Ben,

It gets to the point where it will try to compile a Stan model with stanc.

Can you try to set both STAN_HOME and CMDSTAN_HOME as in below example.

Right now both need to be set. I use CMDSTAN_HOME to run the commands, STAN_HOME to compile a model.

I believe right now, with a standard CmdStan install,  STAN_HOME should always point to a subdir of CMDSTAN_HOME.

Regards,
Rob J. Goedman
goe...@icloud.com

This version of the Stan.jl package assumes that CmdStan (see http://mc-stan.org) is installed and the environment variables STAN_HOME and CMDSTAN_HOME are set accordingly (pointing to the Stan and CmdStan directories, e.g. /Users/rob/Projects/Stan/cmdstan/stan and /Users/rob/Projects/Stan/cmdstan on my system).

