Also, both the effective sample size and the wall time can vary a lot in Stan across different but equivalent ways that the model is parameterized in Stan, and to a lesser extent (hopefully) on starting values, HMC options, etc. With BUGS, there seems to be less variability generally. The schools.stan model that you are using as an example is neither optimized for effective sample size nor wall time. Most of those BUGS examples are primarily intended to illustrate one way to express a familiar model with the Stan language. It takes some practice to express a model in the best way with the Stan language.

