> > Thanks to Dan, Michael and Bob for providing guidance here.  Currently, I have access to an Hadoop platform with an older Cloudera mgmt system, but it sounds like that's not too important at this stage of Stan's development.  To Bob's question of what I'm trying to do, Cleveland's Oct 2013 paper on running R on an Hadoop cluster leveraging a variant of random forests to build an approximate model is what I have in mind.  Based on these comments, I will hack around a bind see if something can be made to work.
> >
> > Thanks again.
> >
> >
> > On Thursday, September 25, 2014 3:54:11 PM UTC-4, Bob Carpenter wrote:
> > We don't provide any out-of-the-box configurations for clusters
> > with Stan.  We've run Stan on clusters for experiments where we
> > want to deal with multiple parameterizatons, models, etc.  It requires
> > some basic cluster-specific config.
> >
